## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply multi-tenant isolation, data governance, and IR planning in a Databricks context beyond generic concepts.

## Key Concepts

- Unity Catalog RBAC and object-level permissions
- Tenant-scoped secret scopes and secret management
- Dynamic data masking and access controls for notebooks
- Audit logs and SIEM integration for detection
- Incident response playbooks and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy enforcement in app layer
function authorize(user, dataset) {
  if (!user.tenants.includes(dataset.tenant)) throw new Error("Access denied");
  // additional masking rules could apply here
  return dataset;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation guarantees across tenants? 
- What metrics and alerts would you instrument to detect leakage or misuse?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate data-security policy into concrete export controls.

## Key Concepts
- Data minimization and redaction
- RBAC and per-session scopes
- Token-based session gating
- Centralized exporting logs and retention
- IR playbooks and containment steps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express route sketch: enforce role-based redaction on export
app.post('/exports/statements', authorize(['viewer','exporter']), (req,res)=>{
  const fields = req.user.role==='exporter' ? fullFields : ['date','amount','balance'];
  const csv = generateCSV(data, fields);
  res.setHeader('Content-Type','text/csv');
  res.send(csv);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the export redaction in CI?
- What metrics indicate success of the control?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of edge ID management, data encryption, and strict multitenant data boundaries across cloud services. It requires concrete controls rather than abstractions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge IAM with audience-bound JWTs and gateway introspection
- Envelope encryption and per-tenant key rotation (KMS)
- Snowflake RBAC + Row-Level Security and per-tenant warehouses
- CI/CD secret scanning and misconfiguration checks
- IR playbooks with traceability and forensics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify JWT audience at edge
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function verify(token, expectedAud) {
  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, KEY, { audience: expectedAud });
    return decoded;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect token reuse across tenants?
- What metrics indicate successful policy enforcement?
